title: Two-way GitHub sync — the enforced foundation (state machine + reconcile brain + sync-layer)
summary: 'Built the foundation for true two-way GitHub sync (Matt''s ask; he chose symmetric reopen + background poll over the conservative recommendations). This round = the enforced backend core. (1) Made done→open a legal REOPEN in the v7 state machine — reopening clears completion/settlement stamps so the learning loop re-settles. (2) Extended SyncProvider with pull()/reopen()/edit() + a provider-agnostic RemoteState (structured fields only, no free-text body → no injection); github flips to pull:true via gh issue view --json. (3) A PURE reconcile() brain: local canonical, applies only legal transitions, surfaces illegal as conflict, symmetric reopen on remote-open+local-done. (4) A sync-layer that applies plans ONLY through updateTask/completeTask/shelveTask (a pull can''t bypass enforcement) + projectTransition for outbound. +20 tests. MCP 468 / CLI 441 green. Next: wire outbound push into CLI+web verbs, POST /api/tasks/sync, CLI task sync, background poll, web strip button.'
