  - packages/paradigm-mcp/src/sync/providers/github.test.ts
  - CHANGELOG.md
learnings:
  - 'The whole two-way design hinges on ONE invariant: a pull NEVER writes raw — it produces a plan that''s applied through the same updateTask/completeTask/shelveTask the CLI/web use, so assertTransition + settlement fire identically. The reconcile() brain is deliberately PURE (no fs/gh) so the enforcement boundary is a single, testable seam.'
  - 'Matt chose symmetric reopen, which required relaxing the v7 ''done is terminal'' invariant (done→open now legal). The safe way to relax it: clear completed/settledAt/crash stamps on reopen so the learning loop can re-settle, rather than leaving a half-settled task. This is a real state-machine semantics change beyond GitHub — documented as such.'
  - RemoteState reads ONLY structured gh --json fields (state/stateReason/labels/assignees), never the issue body/title-into-fields — that's the injection guard baked into the type, not a runtime check.
